== Trivia ==
*'''Bal'''<nowiki>'</nowiki>'''s''' health is displayed as {{HP|???}}.
*'''Bal''' is based on the [https://tolkiengateway.net/wiki/Balrogs Balrog] from J.R.R. Tolkien's ''Lord of the Rings'' series.
**Its spawning place, {{zone|Khazad-dûm}}, is also based on the [https://tolkiengateway.net/wiki/Khazad-dûm place of the same name].
*It used to be possible to trap '''Bal''' by building a cage around its spawn point.
**Building in {{zone|Khazad-dûm}} is now limited in order to prevent this.
*'''Bal''' has fixed invulnerability frames, meaning it will only take damage approximately once every 0.3s{{Confirm}}, even if the player has {{Stat|Attack Speed|100}}, uses {{Stat|Ferocity}} or multiple arrows.
**Certain items such as the {{Item|Souls Rebound}} (currently disabled) or the {{Item|Wither Cloak Sword}} allow players to bypass this.
<!--*'''Bal''' can be easily grinded with a {{Item|Souls Rebound}} and {{Item|Hurricane Bow}}.-->
*'''Bal''' can be [[Corrupted Mobs|corrupted]] via {{Item|Totem of Corruption}}, however no {{Item|Sulphur}} or {{Item|Corrupted Fragment}}s drop.
**{{Item|Totem of Corruption}} has since be changed to only corrupt sea creatures, making it impossible to corrupt '''Bal'''.
*'''Bal''' cannot be damaged by the {{Item|Frozen Scythe}} or {{Item|Glacial Scythe}}.
*The name Bal or Baal originates from proto-Semitic word for "owner" or "master". It got into English through Phoenician, Hebrew, Greek and Latin, where on top of the previously mentioned it gained the meaning "Lord". It is cognate with Beelzebub and Belphegor, two names for the Devil.<ref> https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Baal#English</ref>

== Bugs ==
*'''Bal''' will occasionally fail to respawn. This can be fixed by having all players leave {{Zone|Khazad-dûm}} for a moment.

